{"title":"1958 AHSME Problems/Problem 44","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1958_AHSME_Problems/Problem_44&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Given the true statements: (1) If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> is greater than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" />, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/7/3372c1cb6d68cf97c2d231acc0b47b95a9ed04cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" /> is greater than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/a/96ab646de7704969b91c76a214126b45f2b07b25.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> (2) If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/7/3372c1cb6d68cf97c2d231acc0b47b95a9ed04cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" /> is less than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/a/96ab646de7704969b91c76a214126b45f2b07b25.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/3/a/a3a59bb1293ee3f6dec19de4019a7178874219ae.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$e$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" /> is greater than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/2/bb2c93730dbb48558bb3c4738c956c4e8f816437.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"13\" height=\"18\" />. A valid conclusion is:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/7/9/b7921c2a745baa540c7eac82cc993e888527cfa6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ \\text{If }{a}\\text{ is less than }{b}\\text{, then }{e}\\text{ is greater than }{f}\\qquad \\\\ \\textbf{(B)}\\ \\text{If }{e}\\text{ is greater than }{f}\\text{, then }{a}\\text{ is less than }{b}\\qquad \\\\ \\textbf{(C)}\\ \\text{If }{e}\\text{ is less than }{f}\\text{, then }{a}\\text{ is greater than }{b}\\qquad \\\\ \\textbf{(D)}\\ \\text{If }{a}\\text{ is greater than }{b}\\text{, then }{e}\\text{ is less than }{f}\\qquad \\\\ \\textbf{(E)}\\ \\text{none of these}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"345\" height=\"96\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1958_AHSME_Problems/Problem_44&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>(A) is not valid because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/1/0/710e3e4f18d7c0270ab719a00adc61fa12363b1e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a&lt;b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"43\" height=\"15\" /> does not imply <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/d/c/2dc27b320a46af33b3851ac4f5d74ff926c4ef5b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c\\le d$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"41\" height=\"15\" /> (The inverse of Statement 1 is not necessarily true).\n</p><p>(B) is not valid because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/4/7/f47289328f7183e4ea0fc2999384f47c71fc3554.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$e&gt;f$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"43\" height=\"16\" /> does not imply <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/8/c/e8c4caf5be63fefba3acfbae78c71c7af81bdd8b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c&lt;d$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"41\" height=\"13\" /> (The converse of Statement 2 is not necessarily true either).\n</p><p>In (C), <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/d/6cda58997e68a6d69e51f81d405b80f03af4d156.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$e&lt;f$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"43\" height=\"16\" /> does imply <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/4/a/44ad85b03996171fb031bfc81358c0a07afa10bd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c\\ge d$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"41\" height=\"15\" /> (contrapositive of Statement 2) but this does not tell us anything about <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>In (D), <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/8/2/082852571ecc48ed136ba13dcffa8f6e40064bbd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a&gt;b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"43\" height=\"15\" /> does imply <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/1/9610f673df65a6ad936ecda11d4aa3444437f286.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c&gt;d$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"41\" height=\"13\" />, but the inverse of Statement 2 (<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/8/9/f894aa36aa2853451ed115b89d16e87363253da8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$e\\le f$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"43\" height=\"16\" />) is not necessarily true.\n</p><p>So the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/a/b/1ab2306c569386a84ae40bc666bc52f3b251959a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(E) } \\text{None of these}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"144\" height=\"28\" />.\n(Incidentally, the wording of this problem appears to be wrongly assuming that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/1/6a1615e9f09e5f7da71feb261b0588ea60810f69.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x\\not&lt;y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"43\" height=\"17\" /> implies <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/b/1/7b18737adf5e499e3c33b3c5516930d328ce5a13.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x&gt;y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"43\" height=\"13\" /> (and vice versa) when in reality <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> could be equal. However, this does not change the fact that none of the four choices follow logically from the given statements.)\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1958_AHSME_Problems/Problem_44&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1958_AHSME\" title=\"1958 AHSME\">1958 AHSME</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1958_AHSME_Problems\" title=\"1958 AHSME Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1958_AHSME_Answer_Key\" title=\"1958 AHSME Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=44&amp;year=1958\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1958_AHSME_Problems/Problem_43\